<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ptolemy III Euergetes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 284–<a href="/years/222-bce">222 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ptolemy III Euergetes was king of Ptolemaic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 246 to 222 BCE. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berenice-ii">Berenice II</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magas-of-cyrene">Magas of Cyrene</a>, reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> with Egypt, and the city of Euesperides was refounded as Berenice in her honour. He campaigned deep into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-syrian-war">Third Syrian War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ptolemy-iii-euergetes.jpg" alt="Ptolemy III Euergetes" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:(Venice)_Ancient_Roman_busts_in_the_Museo_archeologico_nazionale_-_Ptolemy_III_Euergetes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
